      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.85
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The region's catastrophic flooding event began with an extreme weather event that pushed reservoirs to capacity. This infrastructure problem led to a hydraulic system breach, with surging flows causing widespread property damage across the geographical areas of Deir Ezzor and Raqqa. The disaster outcome included a bridge collapse and a naval force deploying boats for evacations, ultimately leading to a diplomatic concession from the neighboring country to reduce water releases.",
